.TH EXIST 1.SH NAMEexist, mexist \- test for a file or a module, for scripts.SH SYNOPSIS\fBexist\fR[\-n] [\-d] path.br\fBmexist\fR[\-n] [\-s] module ....SH DESCRIPTIONBoth answer in their exit status, for use in a script, and printnothing.\fBexist\fRreturns 0 when the file exists;\fB\-d\fRasks instead whether it is a directory.\fBmexist\fRreturns 0 when every module named is in the module directory -- thenames are case-sensitive, and up to 256 modules are looked at.\fB\-n\fRturns either test round.\fBmexist \-s\fRlists the modules it passes on the way.  DESIGNA VLT, UTIL 2.40; the helpof\fBexist\fRis in German..SH EXIT STATUSFor\fBexist\fR:\fR0 no error, 17 a wrong argument, 18 no argument, 20 no file name, 21 filenot found..SH EXAMPLES.nfmexist runb; dir        dir runs only if runb is loaded.fi.SH NOTESBoth need Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOgetenv